# SSH Key Authentication

Generate an SSH key:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519
```

This normally creates:

```text
~/.ssh/id_ed25519
~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

Where:

```text
id_ed25519
    -> Private Key

id_ed25519.pub
    -> Public Key
```

### Important Security Rule

```text
PRIVATE KEY
    |
    +---- Keep secret on client

PUBLIC KEY
    |
    +---- Install on target server
          ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

Never copy the private key to the target server.

---

# `authorized_keys`

The target server stores authorized public keys in:

```bash
~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

Example:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
```

Add the public key:

```bash
cat id_ed25519.pub >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

Set permissions:

```bash
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

