# DevOps Perspective — Key Takeaways

### Linux

Linux is one of the most important operating-system environments in DevOps.

### AWS EC2

EC2 provides virtual machines where Linux-based workloads can be deployed and managed.

### SSH

SSH provides secure remote administration.

### Permissions

Linux permissions control access to files and directories.

### Users & Groups

Users and groups provide identity and access management at the operating-system level.

### Package Managers

`apt`, `dnf`, and related package managers simplify software installation and maintenance.

### Shell Scripting

Shell scripts automate repetitive operational tasks.

### Remote Administration

SSH and SCP enable secure server-to-server administration and file transfer.

### Automation

The ultimate DevOps objective is to reduce repetitive manual work through automation.

