## 🔐 Security Reminders

* Never commit `.pem` or private SSH keys to GitHub.
* Never expose passwords or API keys in shell scripts.
* Use least-privilege access.
* Avoid unnecessary `sudo`.
* Be extremely careful with `rm -rf`.
* Restrict AWS Security Group inbound rules.
* Enable MFA on AWS accounts.
* Do not expose SSH (`22`) to the entire internet unless there is a specific reason.
* Prefer key-based authentication over password-based SSH where appropriate.
* Keep operating-system packages updated.

